When forcing a lock or using a pick-axe, Nethack 3.0 will say "You give up
your attempt", or "You stop digging" when a monster appears alongside.  Why
does this not happen when eating?  If one eats some (substantial) food and 
a monster comes along then the monster gets several free shots 
(while you are consuming) before you can respond.
Surely a better response would be to stop eating the food (possibly with some
effect on one's digestive system) so that one can confront the monster.
If I was eating when a minotaur came along I know what I'd worry about first!

A similar thing happens when taking off armor.  In this case it is probably
acceptable not to be able to respond since one is probably too tangled up
to be able to do anything.  In this case a message like

The goblin hits! --more--
You're all tangled up in your +0 chain mail --more--
You can't respond

would be appropriate.

Ken.


